{"kind":"promise","text":"I take NF-10 on branch builder/nf10-device-binding-origin-20261117, stacked on the NF-9 head 6e9acc3a. Where the fact is owned: the platform states the room origin on purpose. loadApplicationScreenContext reads the screen host record and sets context.origin to host.roomOrigin, and readApplicationInvitation matches every invitation's service against that origin. A platform change that gives the screen origin would make the page refuse each invitation, so no deployment-only fix exists. The wrong fact is the Counter's assumption, in deviceSigner (device-key.ts:40), that a device binding names location.origin. The rest of the Counter already uses identity.origin as the room origin (client.ts transports and custody). Change: the device store and deviceSigner take the expected service origin. That is the screen context's origin on an installed screen, and location.origin on the legacy demo page. One case: a binding that names the context origin saves and signs on a different screen host, and a binding that names another origin is refused. Named red against the current check. This is an open Counter 0.6.0 change, so the hosted fix needs a 0.6.0 signing and an install. If you see a platform route I missed, stop me.","body":{"target":"inherit"}}